## Report
Validated the finding against commit 91a5cfe77605f0562415397e0e09392f54f0ab84. This is an information disclosure, so a crash is not expected; I still built the Rust test binary with debuginfo and ran targeted tests. Direct dynamic check: `RUSTFLAGS='-C debuginfo=2' cargo test -p server-http local_debug_bucket_delete_attempt_body_formats_populated_record -- --nocapture` passed. The test constructs a `BucketDeleteDebugSnapshot` with `key: ObjectKey::try_from("root-key\none")` at crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:5183-5186, calls `local_debug_bucket_delete_attempt_body` at serve.rs:5205, and asserts the returned body contains `payload_reclaim_root index=0 object_pg_id=4 key="root-key\none" generation_id=99` at serve.rs:5236-5241. Debugger validation: lldb breakpoint hit `server_http::http::serve::local_debug_bucket_delete_attempt_body` at serve.rs:1160 with a backtrace from `local_debug_bucket_delete_attempt_body_formats_populated_record` at serve.rs:5205. Endpoint/auth path: `handle` returns `local_debug_response` before normal request handling when `local_debug_endpoint` is enabled at serve.rs:691-700. The bucket-delete debug route is `GET /__argmin/debug/bucket-delete-attempt/<bucket>` and returns `local_debug_bucket_delete_attempt_body(&snapshot)` at serve.rs:1041-1067. The debug formatter emits `root.key.as_str()` directly in the HTTP body at serve.rs:1240-1255. Storage population copies `root.key` from `get_bucket_payload_reclaim_root` into `BucketDeleteDebugPayloadReclaimRoot` at crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:11781-11810, and the type explicitly contains `pub key: ObjectKey` at crates/storage/src/types.rs:2532-2537. A second targeted test, `local_debug_metadata_checkpoint_record_endpoint_bypasses_request_admission`, passed and demonstrates enabled local debug endpoints accept a raw HTTP request without S3 auth headers, expecting HTTP 200 at serve.rs:5273-5298. The documentation says these endpoints do not return keys at serve.rs:186-192, so the new payload reclaim root output violates that contract. Scope is limited: argmin-s3 requires the endpoint be enabled and bound to loopback at crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:444-460. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable (`valgrind: command not found`); rust-gdb was unavailable because `gdb` is not installed, but lldb worked.

